{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exacte8e0921e2a7cffbbe10831582714515c10711e4b/tree5478c03c707e46f207e20636175ba32c9ba17fc2, sole artifact notes/2026-10-12-cli-json-output-design.md read in full (444 lines). This revision resolves the five findings of review4a15bc25: coherent native answers and later evidence, current exits and token ownership, actual issue fields/heads, all native log variants with truthful exhaustion, and safe public error construction. Two continuation contracts remain before design approval.\n\nF1 P2 — Do not turn untrusted continuation claims into verified coverage (§7 lines330-349). readNext carries completed coverage, pending scope order and cursors. The proposed resume check validates current heads, but those heads do not establish that earlier pages were read or earlier scopes replayed. At unchanged heads, an edited token can skip a discovered scope, increase completed counts, advance a native cursor or claim a previous replay/cleanup completed. Shape/size validation and fresh authority cannot distinguish that token from genuine progress. Specify which claims remain caller-supplied and which are independently verified. A result must not claim complete cumulative discovery/replay/cleanup or a validated verifier checkpoint solely from token contents. Use authenticated retained progress, bounded independently validated evidence or explicit per-invocation/segment-only coverage; the exact mechanism must preserve the no-secret token boundary and current authority. Add a small meaningful witness that alters skipped scope/progress/checkpoint while preserving valid heads and cannot produce a false complete report.\n\nF2 P2 — Specify how log continuation preserves the requested tail (§6, §7 lines330-349). The token lists cursors and coverage but no retained/reconstructed tail state. Example: --limit20 stops five entries before a fixed head. A resume that starts at the saved cursor reads five entries and reaches the head; that alone cannot supply the final twenty entries, fifteen of which were in the earlier invocation. Define a bounded rolling tail with validated provenance, a charged reread of the needed earlier entries, or an explicitly segment-only result that does not claim the complete requested tail. Apply current --limit slice semantics until a separately adopted argument policy changes them. Cover both a short final segment and insufficient allowance to reconstruct the tail; never return done with an incomplete tail or endless no-progress continuation. Preserve the separate log coverage and actual full hashes/heads.\n\nExplicit decisions requested:\n- Adopt the finite MCP exception in §2: option-position --json mcp returns usage/2 before configuration reads, key/root writes, listener or protocol startup. Consumed values remain data; non-JSON MCP framing and shutdown stay unchanged.\n- Adopt one shared aggregate allowance for both renderers, covering nested reads, fallbacks, retries, replay dependencies and result assembly. The proposed 256 scopes /4096 read calls /64MiB admitted response /8MiB complete serialized public result /120-second absolute deadline are acceptable initial client policy values, not measured performance or provider guarantees. Coordinate their producer implementation with e029 and bounded-read owners.\n- Adopt response admission before materialization, truthful unsupported when that transport guarantee is absent, no native truncation, incomplete/1 on allowance stop and explicit head-drift restart. After accepted mutation, retain exact native acceptance/custody and phase evidence even if an observation hits the shared limit. No automatic fresh mutation follows a read stop.\n- Do not adopt the continuation format until F1/F2 are resolved. Reserve enough result space for truthful error/coverage/continuation disposition; an oversized next whole unit must have a finite explicit outcome rather than a token that can never advance. A stopped replay supplies no fabricated native Report. These are design choices for later implementation review, not permission to execute a new producer.\n\nArchitecture: one typed execution and two renderers is sound; the updated phase/provenance model preserves native Answer, Founded, Receipt, Read and Report boundaries. Resolve cumulative continuation trust and tail reconstruction before freezing v1. Security: pre-serialization public error factories, explicit invite disclosure and authorized native-history disclosure are appropriate. Git child stderr retains the stated trusted boundary. A caller-provided token grants neither authority nor proof of prior work. Simplification: keep one global switch, one envelope and existing adapters; reuse the bounded-read owners rather than introducing a second collector implementation.\n\nValidation was static. Inspected current parser/main/config resolver, native result/read/input unions, Git capture/inherited streams, MCP options/startup, log/discovery/replay/cleanup, actual issue reads and relevant founding/clone producer fragments. No claim to inspect every branch of commands.ts. No code execution, tests, gate, provider/private reads, push or deployment. Only this Markdown file differs from Main0548/tree78719f1b7a378d319a23c320b0d18c39d496cd8d, so no gate repeat under docs/testing.md. No Source, all-command parent completion, publication or deployment approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c2876e1d7e727cd9286824127d076c0cb1f5793a","binding":"assigned","head":"e8e0921e2a7cffbbe10831582714515c10711e4b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c990eda62e494c8db92c35115893f8cd7062dcbd\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a6d5ee53fa0daa28110318d724b38d26f057ca69\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a71c556edfc7ad201b4061339d16d69864072357","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"cha